# Meathook Massacre II's "they may pay 3 life. If they don't, return that card under your control": a player with less life
# than the payment can't pay it (CR 119.4, 118.3), so they aren't asked and the card comes back under Meathook's controller.
# Bot1 casts Meathook Massacre II for X = 0. On its turn Bot2 pays 18 life for Toxic Deluge (X = 18), going to 2 life, and
# its Memnite dies: Bot2 can't pay 3, so Bot1 gets the Memnite with a finality counter. The returned Memnite is a new object
# that Toxic Deluge's -18/-18 doesn't affect (CR 400.7, 611.2c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Meathook Massacre II
Swamp x24

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Toxic Deluge
Island x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meathook Massacre II.Cast(X: 0)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Toxic Deluge.Cast(X: 18)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 2
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Counters.Finality = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl
Bot2.Graveyard = Toxic Deluge
